{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9194-1","published":"2026-11-25T02:38:24Z","modified":"2026-11-25T21:43:18.592956422Z","upstream":["CVE-2016-7949","CVE-2016-7950","CVE-2026-88807","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-7949","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-7950","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-88807"],"summary":"libxrender vulnerabilities","details":"Adam Bedard discovered that libXrender incorrectly handled certain\nresponses from an X server, resulting in a heap buffer overflow. If a user\nwere tricked into connecting to a malicious X server, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause applications using libXrender to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-88807)\n\nTobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXrender did not correctly validate\nlengths in responses from an X server. An attacker controlling an X server\ncould possibly use these issues to cause applications using libXrender to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code. This\nupdate provides the fixes for Ubuntu 14.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7949,\nCVE-2016-7950)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libxrender","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:14.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libxrender?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Ftrusty"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:0.9.8-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]}],"versions":["1:0.9.8-1","1:0.9.8-1build0.14.04.1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libxrender1","binary_version":"1:0.9.8-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:14.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-9194-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libxrender","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libxrender?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:0.9.9-0ubuntu1+esm2"}]}],"version